# A Chromebook has no function row: the top row emits action keys, which keyd
# (/etc/keyd/default.conf) passes on as the XF86 keysyms Omarchy binds. This
# tells the keybindings menu which physical key each of those keysyms sits on,
# so it shows the action row's legends instead of a function row the keyboard
# does not have.
#
# Format: <keysym> <name>, both ^[A-Za-z0-9_]+$; one per line, '#' comments.
XF86MonBrightnessDown F6
XF86MonBrightnessUp F7
XF86AudioMute F8
XF86AudioLowerVolume F9
XF86AudioRaiseVolume F10
